6,-9,-4,-5,6],[-6,-9,-5,6,-4],[-6,-9,-5,-4,6],[-6,6,-9,-4,-5],[-6,6,-9,-5,-4],[-6,6,-4,-9,-5],[-6,6,-4,-5,-9],[-6,6,-5,-9,-4],[-6,6,-5,-4,-9],[-6,-4,-9,6,-5],[-6,-4,-9,-5,6],[-6,-4,6,-9,-5],[-6,-4,6,-5,-9],[-6,-4,-5,-9,6],[-6,-4,-5,6,-9],[-6,-5,-9,6,-4],[-6,-5,-9,-4,6],[-6,-5,6,-9,-4],[-6,-5,6,-4,-9],[-6,-5,-4,-9,6],[-6,-5,-4,6,-9],[-9,-6,6,-4,-5],[-9,-6,6,-5,-4],[-9,-6,-4,6,-5],[-9,-6,-4,-5,6],[-9,-6,-5,6,-4],[-9,-6,-5,-4,6],[-9,6,-6,-4,-5],[-9,6,-6,-5,-4],[-9,6,-4,-6,-5],[-9,6,-4,-5,-6],[-9,6,-5,-6,-4],[-9,6,-5,-4,-6],[-9,-4,-6,6,-5],[-9,-4,-6,-5,6],[-9,-4,6,-6,-5],[-9,-4,6,-5,-6],[-9,-4,-5,-6,6],[-9,-4,-5,6,-6],[-9,-5,-6,6,-4],[-9,-5,-6,-4,6],[-9,-5,6,-6,-4],[-9,-5,6,-4,-6],[-9,-5,-4,-6,6],[-9,-5,-4,6,-6],[6,-6,-9,-4,-5],[6,-6,-9,-5,-4],[6,-6,-4,-9,-5],[6,-6,-4,-5,-9],[6,-6,-5,-9,-4],[6,-6,-5,-4,-9],[6,-9,-6,-4,-5],[6,-9,-6,-5,-4],[6,-9,-4,-6,-5],[6,-9,-4,-5,-6],[6,-9,-5,-6,-4],[6,-9,-5,-4,-6],[6,-4,-6,-9,-5],[6,-4,-6,-5,-9],[6,-4,-9,-6,-5],[6,-4,-9,-5,-6],[6,-4,-5,-6,-9],[6,-4,-5,-9,-6],[6,-5,-6,-9,-4],[6,-5,-6,-4,-9],[6,-5,-9,-6,-4],[6,-5,-9,-4,-6],[6,-5,-4,-6,-9],[6,-5,-4,-9,-6],[-4,-6,-9,6,-5],[-4,-6,-9,-5,6],[-4,-6,6,-9,-5],[-4,-6,6,-5,-9],[-4,-6,-5,-9,6],[-4,-6,-5,6,-9],[-4,-9,-6,6,-5],[-4,-9,-6,-5,6],[-4,-9,6,-6,-5],[-4,-9,6,-5,-6],[-4,-9,-5,-6,6],[-4,-9,-5,6,-6],[-4,6,-6,-9,-5],[-4,6,-6,-5,-9],[-4,6,-9,-6,-5],[-4,6,-9,-5,-6],[-4,6,-5,-6,-9],[-4,6,-5,-9,-6],[-4,-5,-6,-9,6],[-4,-5,-6,6,-9],[-4,-5,-9,-6,6],[-4,-5,-9,6,-6],[-4,-5,6,-6,-9],[-4,-5,6,-9,-6],[-5,-6,-9,6,-4],[-5,-6,-9,-4,6],[-5,-6,6,-9,-4],[-5,-6,6,-4,-9],[-5,-6,-4,-9,6],[-5,-6,-4,6,-9],[-5,-9,-6,6,-4],[-5,-9,-6,-4,6],[-5,-9,6,-6,-4],[-5,-9,6,-4,-6],[-5,-9,-4,-6,6],[-5,-9,-4,6,-6],[-5,6,-6,-9,-4],[-5,6,-6,-4,-9],[-5,6,-9,-6,-4],[-5,6,-9,-4,-6],[-5,6,-4,-6,-9],[-5,6,-4,-9,-6],[-5,-4,-6,-9,6],[-5,-4,-6,6,-9],[-5,-4,-9,-6,6],[-5,-4,-9,6,-6],[-5,-4,6,-6,-9],[-5,-4,6,-9,-6]]},{"args":[[0,-10]],"expected":[[0,-10],[-10,0]]}],"gen":"(r, big) => [r.distinct(big ? 6 : r.int(1, 5), -10, 10)]","hints":["Fill the positions from left to right. What can go in the first position? And in the second, once the first is fixed?","Any number not used yet can go next. Unlike subsets, there is no start index: a number to the left of the last one picked is still allowed.","Keep a used[] array. For each i not used: mark it, push nums[i], recurse, then pop and unmark. When cur has n numbers, record a copy."],"explain":{"intuition":"<p>Use the same template as for subsets, but the tree has a different shape. A node is a partial ordering; its children append one more number that is <b>not used yet</b>. There is no start index, because order matters now: after picking 5 you may still pick 0, and <code>[5, 0, …]</code> is a different answer from <code>[0, 5, …]</code>. Only the <b>leaves</b>, where all n numbers are placed, are answers. The tree has n choices at the top, n − 1 below, and so on, so n! leaves.</p>\n<p>To know which numbers are free, keep a boolean array <code>used</code>. It is part of the state, so it follows the same rule as <code>cur</code>: set it when you choose, clear it when you un-choose. Forget to clear it and every later branch thinks that number is already placed.</p>","steps":["Keep <code>cur</code>, <code>out</code> and <code>used = [false] * n</code>.","<code>go()</code>: if <code>cur.length === n</code>, record a copy and return.","For each <code>i</code> with <code>used[i]</code> false: set <code>used[i] = true</code>, push <code>nums[i]</code>, call <code>go()</code>, pop, set <code>used[i] = false</code>.","Call <code>go()</code>. There are n! answers."],"pitfalls":["Clearing <code>cur</code> but not <code>used</code> on the way back. After the first leaf, no number is free and the search stops with one answer.","Reusing the subsets loop with a start index. That only builds increasing-position lists, so it returns one ordering instead of n!.","Checking <code>cur.includes(nums[i])</code> instead of a used array. It works for distinct numbers but costs O(n) per check."],"complexity":{"time":"O(n · n!): n! orderings, each copied in O(n)","space":"O(n) besides the output"}},"solutions":[{"title":"Backtracking with a used array","idea":"Fill positions left to right. Any number not used yet may go next. Mark it on the way in and unmark it on the way out.","time":"O(n · n!)","space":"O(n) besides the output","ts":"function allOrderings(nums: number[]): number[][] {\n  const n = nums.length;\n  const out: number[][] = [];\n  const cur: number[] = [];\n  const used = new Array<boolean>(n).fill(false);\n  const go = (): void => {\n    if (cur.length === n) { out.push([...cur]); return; }\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      if (used[i]) continue;\n      used[i] = true; cur.push(nums[i]);  // choose\n      go();                               // explore\n      cur.pop(); used[i] = false;         // un-choose both\n    }\n  };\n  go();\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def allOrderings(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n        n = len(nums)\n        out, cur, used = [], [], [False] * n\n\n        def go() -> None:\n            if len(cur) == n:\n                out.append(cur[:])\n                return\n            for i in range(n):\n                if used[i]:\n                    continue\n                used[i] = True\n                cur.append(nums[i])  # choose\n                go()                 # explore\n                cur.pop()\n                used[i] = False      # un-choose both\n\n        go()\n        return out","js":"function allOrderings(nums) {\n  const n = nums.length;\n  const out = [];\n  const cur = [];\n  const used = new Array(n).fill(false);\n  const go = () => {\n    if (cur.length === n) {\n      out.push([...cur]);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      if (used[i]) continue;\n      used[i] = true;\n      cur.push(nums[i]);\n      go();\n      cur.pop();\n      used[i] = false;\n    }\n  };\n  go();\n  return out;\n}"},{"title":"Swap into place","idea":"Positions 0..k−1 are fixed. Swap each candidate from k..n−1 into position k, recurse on k + 1, then swap back. No extra arrays.","time":"O(n · n!)","space":"O(n) besides the output","ts":"function allOrderings(nums: number[]): number[][] {\n  const a = [...nums];\n  const out: number[][] = [];\n  const go = (k: number): void => {\n    if (k === a.length) { out.push([...a]); return; }\n    for (let i = k; i < a.length; i++) {\n      [a[k], a[i]] = [a[i], a[k]]; // put a[i] at position k\n      go(k + 1);\n      [a[k], a[i]] = [a[i], a[k]]; // swap back\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def allOrderings(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n        a = nums[:]\n        out = []\n\n        def go(k: int) -> None:\n            if k == len(a):\n                out.append(a[:])\n                return\n            for i in range(k, len(a)):\n                a[k], a[i] = a[i], a[k]  # put a[i] at position k\n                go(k + 1)\n                a[k], a[i] = a[i], a[k]  # swap back\n\n        go(0)\n        return out","js":"function allOrderings(nums) {\n  const a = [...nums];\n  const out = [];\n  const go = (k) => {\n    if (k === a.length) {\n      out.push([...a]);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (let i = k; i < a.length; i++) {\n      [a[k], a[i]] = [a[i], a[k]];\n      go(k + 1);\n      [a[k], a[i]] = [a[i], a[k]];\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}"}],"followups":["The list may now contain repeated values, and each different ordering must appear once. What do you skip, and why does it need sorting?","Produce only the next ordering in lexicographic order, in place and in O(n). How do you find what to change?"],"related":[],"kind":"function","nEx":3,"nBig":2,"lcTitle":"Permutations","acc":0.008243515942702132,"co":[["Workday",92,180],["Arista Networks",71,0],["Booking.com",70,0],["Microstrategy",69,0],["Zomato",62,0],["Qualcomm",58,0],["Amazon",57,30],["LinkedIn",57,0],["Microsoft",55,90],["Infosys",54,180],["American Express",53,0],["Samsung",53,0],["Epic Systems",51,0],["Bloomberg",50,90],["TikTok",50,0],["Google",49,90],["Citadel",47,0],["Apple",46,0],["Meta",43,180],["tcs",42,0],["Visa",39,0],["Uber",35,0],["Oracle",27,0],["Goldman Sachs",21,0]]}